On Wednesday, June 3, 2015 at 9:48:02 AM UTC-4, Michael Betancourt wrote:
> All of the BBVB tuning parameters, for one.  But eventually also possibly
> the variation distribution, or the exact variational algorithm or how the
> variation expectations are reported on the constrained scale.

But those are all aspects of the VB config. It would specify all the tuning parameters that are VB-specific. And we could add flags to it as necessary to select the variation distribution or how it is minimized. I think how the expectations are reported would be a print option, but in principle that could be part of the VB config too.

I just don't see the utility of having the user call

config <- new("stan_vb_config")
stan_vb(program, config)
stan_hmc(program, config) # error

when that config already implies the VB approach and is only valid input for a stan_vb() function.

Ben

