Subject: Re: [stan-dev] C++ namesapces: <cmath> is std:: <cmath>, <math.h> is ::
Message-ID: <YQ1pdMcnxbI.13RVURmyyFIJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <YQ1pdMcnxbI.oiy8cy7bzMcJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
References: <YQ1pdMcnxbI.oiy8cy7bzMcJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/YQ1pdMcnxbI/m/13RVURmyyFIJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Note:  Boost by default configures these functions to throw exceptions,
whereas the <math.h> versions just silently return NaN.  I think
the exceptions are a good thing --- throw a warning at the earliest
sign of arithmetic trouble.

- Bob

