Yes, a test-suite would make a lot of sense. To report back: the cvode runs are far slower, but they seem to run more consistent, i.e. all chains progress at a very similar pace. The runs are not yet completed, I will report back once the runs are over.

This puzzles me a bit, I hope cvode can be run in a faster way (I already went to 1e-6 absolute and relative tolerances). @Tom: Any suggestions? What parameters are important to take care of (Stan wise and cvode wise)?

Out of curiosity: Is it thinkable to get

http://headmyshoulder.github.io/odeint-v2/doc/boost_numeric_odeint/tutorial/parallel_computation_with_openmp_and_mpi.html

up and running in Stan with the good old boost odeint integrator? The instructions sound very straightforward or am I overlooking something which prevents openMP for ODE solving in Stan fundamentally? Usually I get to hear "autodiff" is the killer, but isn't this now separate enough from autodiff?

Best,
Sebastian

