> What about keeping the contract between the client interface (RStan,
> PyStan, etc.) and Stan as simple as possible?

The contract will be pretty simple — the question is how much duplication
we require of the user or how much type information we utilize in the var
context.

> Could one allow Stan to
> pass error messages if something goes wrong? Perhaps we could just reuse
> here whatever pattern we're going to use with error handling for the
> sampler arguments?

Right now it’s all exceptions that get caught and turned into error messages
by the model class.

> (Why can't one use functions like `contains_r_only` to check types?)

That just checks reals vs ints.  I’m thinking about checking vectors vs
matrices vs scalars.

> p.s. "client interface" is a reasonable generic term for RStan, PyStan,
> etc., right?

I think RStan etc are just referred to as “clients" of the Stan API.

